Results File
prmr_v01_results.json

This file contains:

Full state trajectory across all epochs
Information and fitness evolution
Genealogy (merger history)
Domain-specific results
Key Metrics Explained
N_max
Maximum number of recursive cycles before termination
Information (I)
Tracks how system content evolves over time
Fitness (Φ)
Measures organised complexity:
higher values → more structured systems
Vortex Count
Indicates system expansion and structural complexity
Genealogy Tree (H)
Tracks lineage of structures through mergers
Reproducibility

The simulation uses a fixed random seed:

seed = 42

This ensures consistent and reproducible results across runs.

Customising Parameters

Key parameters can be modified in the code:

eta = 0.10          # information loss rate
a_crit = 100.0      # fragmentation threshold
omega_crit = 0.20   # survival threshold
d_merge = 8.0       # merge distance

Changing these values allows exploration of:

growth vs collapse behaviour
stability regimes
structural emergence patterns


Notes
This version (v0.01) is a conceptual computational framework
The model is not yet physically validated
Parameters are chosen to demonstrate behaviour, not to represent real-world systems
Future versions will refine:
